	title = "High Order",
	category = "group",
	region = "zephras-isle",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
		{ type = "quest", id = 92596 },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The High Order are the magisters of the {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link}, the descendants of the Highborne scholars of Eldre'Thalas. They call themselves the keepers of the Highborne ways. Over ten thousand years in {link:skywall}Skywall{/link} much of their arcane lore was forgotten, and their power waned. They mean to recover it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Their Creed",
			text = [=[The High Order holds that the {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link} made a grave mistake when they placed their fate in the hands of fickle spirits. The spirits' vanishing proved it. What the spirits once did, the order believes, can be done with the magic of the {red:highborne}Highborne{/red}, and the island can stand on its own. They study the risen ley lines of {link:zephras-isle}Zephras{/link} and the elemental magic of the standing stones, whatever the {link:windshapers}Windshapers{/link} say. To the Windshapers they are meddlers. To themselves they are the only ones willing to act.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The Supreme Magister {link:elaadrin-evengale}Elaadrin Evengale{/link} found a way to peer through the planes, and found the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} looking back. Through the Kirin Tor the High Order has joined the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}. Its young magisters now sail from {link:valanaar}Valanaar{/link} to Dalaran to reclaim the knowledge their ancestors lost.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "al-aketh",
	title = "Al'Aketh",
	aliases = { "Al'Aketh Cult", "cult of Al'Akir" },
	category = "group",
	region = "zephras-isle",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
		{ type = "target" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Al'Aketh are a cult of {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link} who worship {link:al-akir}Al'Akir{/link} the Windlord. Some of their founders used their skysight to look across {link:skywall}Skywall{/link} and glimpsed the terrible might of its master. Tempted by that power, they broke from their people and gave themselves to his service. When the {link:vanishing-of-the-wind-spirits}wind spirits{/link} vanished, the cult rose in the fear that followed.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Their Creed",
			text = [=[The cult preaches that the {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link} grew proud and idle, taking the gifts of the winds for granted, and that the spirits left them for it. Only penance and service to the {link:al-akir}Windlord{/link} will bring the wind back. Its missionaries play at being a gentle faith. Its brutes, stormcallers and assassins do the rest. Many of its members were once {link:windshapers}Windshapers{/link}, peacekeepers or druids, and {link:ayessa-dawnsinger}Ayessa Dawnsinger{/link} calls the cult a dark mirror of her own order.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Under {link:high-priestess-lorthuna}High Priestess Lorthuna{/link} the cult held {link:falaath-village}Falaath Village{/link} and the {link:shrine-of-akir}Shrine of Akir{/link}, raided the island's caravans, and struck at the pylon watchtowers to bring down the wards that hid {link:zephras-isle}Zephras{/link}. Its high priestess is gone and its shrine has been stormed, but its purpose was fulfilled. The {link:al-akir}Windlord{/link}'s servants now know where Zephras lies.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "peacekeepers",
	title = "Peacekeepers",
	aliases = { "Peacekeeper" },
	category = "group",
	region = "zephras-isle",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Peacekeepers are the militia of {link:zephras-isle}Zephras Isle{/link} and the closest thing the {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link} have to an army. They answer to Captain {link:valennia-stormfist}Valennia Stormfist{/link} in {link:valanaar}Valanaar{/link} and to {link:shadow-council}the Council{/link} of Elders. Their constables keep order in the villages, and their soldiers man the watchtowers that guard the {link:anchor-pylons}anchor pylons{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[For long the Peacekeepers avoided open war with the {link:al-aketh}Al'Aketh{/link}, hoping the cult would stay a nuisance. That hope ended at {link:shen-dar-village}Shen'dar Village{/link} and the pylon watchtowers. Few in number, they fought the cult across the island and led the assault on the {link:shrine-of-akir}Shrine of Akir{/link}. They also stand between the {link:windshapers}Windshapers{/link} and the {link:high-order}High Order{/link}, and their captain will not suffer the two orders to fight in {link:valanaar}Valanaar{/link}. Not all of them stayed true. {link:commander-belguilos}Belguilos{/link}, whom the cult now calls the Breaker, once wore their colors. Among those who held were {link:constable-aonda}Constable Aonda{/link} of Shen'dar, the lieutenant {link:yorana-windyreed}Yorana Windyreed{/link} at the eastern tower, and {link:hyusaa-quickbreeze}Hyusaa Quickbreeze{/link}, the captain's second.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "anchor-pylons",
	title = "Anchor Pylons",
	aliases = { "anchor pylon", "anchor pylons", "wind pylons" },
	category = "structure",
	region = "zephras-isle",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
		{ type = "quest", id = 94414 },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The anchor pylons are ancient towers of elemental magic, gifts of the {link:vanishing-of-the-wind-spirits}wind spirits{/link} to the {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link}. They bind {link:zephras-isle}Zephras Isle{/link} together and hold it in its place in {link:skywall}Skywall{/link}. Watchtowers of the {link:peacekeepers}Peacekeepers{/link} stand beside them, one in the western highlands and one outside {link:valanaar}Valanaar{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Their Failing",
			text = [=[Since the spirits vanished, the pylons have grown unstable. Their splendor has not changed, and no damage can be seen, but their magic falters. As it weakens, parts of the island crumble and fall into the sky. The {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link} now draw on windstones to meet their daily needs, and the {link:high-order}High Order{/link} hopes to master the pylons' magic before it fails for good.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Wards",
			text = [=[The {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link} had half forgotten a second purpose. The pylons are also wards. They shielded the island from the gaze of whatever else dwells in {link:skywall}Skywall{/link}. The {link:flight-from-eldre-thalas}Shal'nan{/link} once spoke of it, and the {link:al-aketh}Al'Aketh{/link} learned it. They struck at the pylons to bring the wards down, and they succeeded. {link:zephras-isle}Zephras{/link} still floats, but it is hidden no longer.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "vanishing-of-the-wind-spirits",
	title = "Vanishing of the Wind Spirits",
	aliases = { "wind spirits" },
	category = "event",
	region = "zephras-isle",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[For thousands of years, spirits of the wind lived on {link:zephras-isle}Zephras Isle{/link} beside the {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link}, as patrons, teachers and friends. They raised the island, tended its magic and gave its seers the skysight. Then, several centuries ago, they vanished. They gave no warning, and no one on Zephras knows why they went or where.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "What Followed",
			text = [=[The island's magic began to fade. The {link:anchor-pylons}anchor pylons{/link} faltered. Most of the spirits' constructs stopped working. Strange pale spirits called hollows appeared in the {link:shadowgale-forest}Shadowgale Forest{/link}. Beasts grew wild, and the lesser sprites of the wind turned violent when stirred. Contact with the other isles was lost, and whole villages fell into the sky. Each faction read the loss in its own way. The {link:windshapers}Windshapers{/link} wish to find the spirits and call them home. The {link:high-order}High Order{/link} says the elves must never again depend on them. The {link:al-aketh}Al'Aketh{/link} preach that the spirits abandoned a proud people, and that only the {link:al-akir}Windlord{/link} remains.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "flight-from-eldre-thalas",
	title = "Flight from Eldre'Thalas",
	aliases = { "Rebellion in Eldre'Thalas", "Shal'nan" },
	category = "event",
	region = "zephras-isle",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link} began as rebels. After the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, the {red:highborne}Highborne{/red} of Eldre'Thalas, the city in {link:feralas}Feralas{/link} now called {red:dire-maul}Dire Maul{/red}, were left without the Well that had fed their magic. Prince {red:tortheldrin}Tortheldrin{/red} sought to sustain them with ever darker powers. Some of his people had seen where such hunger led, and they would not let {link:azshara}Azshara{/link}'s mistakes be made again.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Veiled One",
			text = [=[The rebels were led by a figure known only as the Shal'nan, the Veiled One, who hid his face behind a featureless mask of gold. His name became a battle cry. Through sabotage and worse, his followers hampered the prince's network of crystal foci and shamed him again and again. In those days the druidism of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} of the north also spread through the city, and the prince condemned it as base. The rebels made their last stand in his sanctum. They averted the worst, but most of them died.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Flight",
			text = [=[The survivors fled west with the prince's fleet behind them. Beyond the sea they found a land ruled by ancient spirits, and there they struck their pact with the wind. The spirits raised the land into {link:skywall}Skywall{/link}, and the exiles became the {link:skyborne}shen'dorei{/link}, the hidden people. In time the Shal'nan laid down his rule and gave it to a council chosen by his people.]=],
		},
	},
})
